                <pb facs="0805" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00/252: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-04T08:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 4, 1919, 8
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.28
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Four o’clock this morning President Pardo was seized in the Palace and is now
                    imprisoned in penitentiary. Incidental to movement <pb facs="0806" n="721"
                        xml:id="pg721"/> two soldiers killed and three wounded, including minor
                    official. Minister of War and Minister of Government also in prison. Chief of
                    Staff of Navy in prison, Chief of Staff of the Army escaped with 40 men. Prefect
                    of Callao in prison and new prefect in power.</p>
                <p>Leguia’s followers instigators of [<hi rendition="#italic">coup d’état</hi>].</p>
                <p>As it is customary for the government in power to send official representative to
                    fourth July reception at the Legation, have called off large reception prepared
                    for this afternoon to avoid possible complications which would come from
                    receiving or declining to receive representative of new regime.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
